/*
 * cbvmc_resident_ipl: the resident half of the IPL install (G4 stage 1, docs/virtual_memory_card.md).  PowerPC, freestanding.  Original work.
 *
 * What it is: the card store of the IPL runtime, READ/WRITE since 2026-11-06 (before: read-only).  Same chain as the game path: both cards on one
 * journalled write-back window (a power cut leaves the files consistent), the Flippy file API below it with no handle kept open between calls
 * (IPL rule).  A missing card file is generated by the installer; a pending journal is replayed.  Everything below this line that still says
 * "read-only" describes the first G4 builds.  Old description: the card store of the IPL runtime, READ-ONLY.  The two card files are opened once, read-only (Flippy open flags without the write bit),
 * and every read of the card model goes to the drive through the same polled, DI-preserving driver the game path uses.  Every write, create, rename or
 * remove that the model asks for is REFUSED (counted, answered with an I/O error): the model then reports an erase/program error in the card's status
 * register, BS2's own CARD library turns that into its I/O-error result, and nothing reaches the SD.  There is no write-back window, no journal file
 * is created or replayed (a PENDING journal makes that slot not served: start a game once, its install image replays it), nothing is ever formatted or
 * generated.  The only files this image writes are two small text files of its own: /cubeboot/cbvmc_ipl_status.txt (at install) and
 * /cubeboot/cbvmc_ipl_counters.txt (at hand-over to a game).
 *
 * Test build (-DCBVMC_TEST_RAM, Dolphin): the same store over a RAM card the harness provides, no drive, no files.
 */
